- there are as many TYPES OF QUESTIONS as components in the information;

- for each type there are THREE LEVELS OF READING: the elementary level, the intermediate level, and the overall level;

- any question can be defined by its type and level.

These reading levels are comparable to the integrative levels of the mind. Their analysis permits knowing in advance the totality of the questions which any given information can generate; as a result it permits studying the probability of their occurrence and, if appropriate, of taking them into account in the graphic construction.
